      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">امهر المَرْأَةَ</span></b> : see 1, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">امهر النَّاقَةَ</span>
<i>He called,</i> or <i>rendered,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَعَلَ</span>) <i>the she-camel a</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَهْرِيَّة</span>: (K:) [it has sometimes, if not always,
the latter meaning; for] it is said of the breaker,
or trainer; and is like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْحَلَهَا</span>. (TA, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رحل</span>.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">امهرت الفَرَسُ</span> <i>The mare had a colt following
her.</i> (TA.)

